0. Definitions
   "Software" means Codex Design: its source code, studios (3D Workshop, Texture Studio, VFX Studio, GFX Studio),
   SDK, scripts, documentation, training material and bundled libraries authored by AstraServices.
   "Outputs" means anything produced with the Software: models, textures, materials, VFX packages, Luau code,
   images, videos, renders and other exported files.
   "You" means the person or entity using the Software.
   "Commercial Use" means use intended for, or directed toward, commercial advantage or monetary compensation,
   including: selling or licensing Outputs; using Outputs in a monetized game or experience (for example Roblox
   experiences with paid items, game passes, developer products, subscriptions or ads); asset stores; client or
   contract work; and paid services built on the Software.

1. Acceptance. By downloading, installing, running or otherwise using the Software, You accept this license. If
   You do not accept it, do not use the Software.

2. Permitted use. You may download, install and run the Software for personal, educational, evaluation and other
   non-commercial purposes, and use Outputs for the same purposes.

3. No modification or redistribution without permission. Without prior written permission from AstraServices You
   may not:
   a) modify, translate, adapt or create derivative works of the source code;
   b) publish, redistribute, sublicense, sell, rent or host the Software or modified versions of it, in whole or
      in part, including forks published to public repositories or package registries (forking on GitHub solely
      as required to view the code is not a permitted redistribution channel for modified versions);
   c) remove or alter copyright notices or this license.

4. Ownership of Outputs.
   a) AstraServices keeps all rights in the Software, including code, templates, procedural recipes, textures,
      examples and other material of the Software that appears in Outputs.
   b) This license does not transfer to AstraServices any rights You hold in Your own original contribution to an
      Output (for example Your own designs, artwork or recipes). Whether and to what extent an Output is protected
      by copyright depends on the human contribution, third-party material used and the applicable law.
   c) Independently of who owns an Output, Your right to use the Software is granted on the condition that Outputs
      are not put to Commercial Use without permission under section 6. This is a contractual condition of this
      license, not a claim of ownership over Your original contribution.

5. Provenance metadata.
   a) Outputs carry machine-readable provenance metadata (for example PNG text chunks, glTF/GLB asset fields, EXR
      header attributes, Roblox file comments and manifests, Luau headers), and export file names may contain
      "_CodexDesign". Nothing visible is added to the content itself.
   b) You may not intentionally remove, alter or forge this metadata in order to hide that an Output was made with
      the Software.
   c) Loss of metadata caused by ordinary conversion or processing that cannot preserve it (for example importing
      a GLB into Roblox as a MeshPart, image re-encoding by a platform, renaming files) is not a breach of this
      license.

6. Commercial permission.
   a) Commercial Use of the Software or of Outputs requires a separate written permission from AstraServices.
   b) Each permission defines its own scope: covered projects or experiences, territory, duration, whether it is
      exclusive, transferable or sublicensable, and any fee or attribution. What a permission does not expressly
      grant stays reserved.
   c) Permissions are requested at https://github.com/AstraServices/Codex-Design (open an issue or contact the
      owner). A permission is only valid when confirmed in writing by AstraServices.

7. Asset packs and products sold by AstraServices. Models, textures, VFX and other assets that AstraServices
   distributes or sells (for example asset packs) are licensed under the terms that come with each product. Those
   terms, not section 2 or 6 of this license, decide what buyers may do with those assets, including Commercial Use
   in their own games. Buying such a product does not grant any right to the Software itself.

8. Third-party material. Bundled third-party assets (icon packs, VFX packs and others under assets/) remain under
   their own licenses, which are listed with them. This license does not grant rights the third parties did not
   grant, and their terms apply in addition to this one.

9. Termination.
   a) If You breach this license, AstraServices may notify You. If You cure the breach within 30 days after that
      notice, Your rights continue. Rights end automatically if the breach is not cured in that time, or at once for
      a repeated breach or an intentional removal of provenance metadata to hide the origin of Outputs.
   b) After termination You must stop using the Software. Outputs already used for non-commercial purposes before
      termination may stay where they are, but may not be put to new Commercial Use. Outputs covered by a written
      commercial permission remain governed by that permission.
   c) AstraServices may reinstate Your rights in writing.
   d) Sections 4, 5, 7, 8, 10 and 11 survive termination.

